From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 14:41:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sx8): close the R53 check gate -- same-run verifier
 receipt + companion identity guard (lane-242)

CHECK-R53-FABLE.md returned PASS-GATED on two findings. Both are closed here.

Finding 1 -- the same-run check was written and never run. Every PPL figure in the report hangs on whether the id57 GGUF's S-X8 blocks and the HF container's blocks are the same quantization run; if they are not, the extracted bases/scales do not belong to the GGUF's coefficient bytes and the numbers are an artefact. tools/sx8/verify_gguf_matches_container.py has now been run on both the smallest and the largest S-X8 tensor. All six block fields (dmin, dmax, config, levels_hi, levels_lo, coeff) are byte-identical across 20.6M blocks. VERDICT: SAME quantization run, EXIT=0. Receipt r53-evidence/40-verify-gguf-matches-container.txt, script r53-verify40.cmd.

Finding 2 -- no mismatched-companion guard. create_tensor matched companion tensors by name and shape alone, so a companion built from a different quantization of the same architecture attached silently and paired foreign b0/b1 with these c0/c1, corrupting every S-X8 matmul. add_sx8_pca_to_gguf.py now stamps the source model's identity into the companion (sx8pca.source.name/.tensor/.head) and llama-model-loader.cpp:959-1029 compares the stamp against the same bytes read from the model being loaded, throwing on mismatch.

Two deliberate deviations from the check's sketch, stated for HQ: (a) raw head bytes compared directly, not a sha256 KV -- libllama does not link vendor/hash/sha256 and a CMake change cannot be validated in a pass that may not build, and comparing the bytes is strictly stronger than comparing a hash of them; (b) a companion with no identity keys warns and loads rather than throwing -- the companion of record on disk predates this change, and refusing it would break HQ's first build and smoke.

UNBUILT and UNRUN: the C++ is not compiled (another maker owns the GPU and the build tree this pass) and no companion carrying the new KVs has been written. HQ builds and gates both at integration; report section 4a and owed item 11 say so.

Docs corrections from the check's remaining findings, in the report and the registry row: the -0.034% PPL delta is now stated as sign only, indistinguishable from zero (it is ~5% of one cell's stderr, and the 4-chunk smoke and the 8-chunk float-route probe have the opposite sign); 30a-route-probe.log is cited, ruling out the Q8_1 activation route as the masker; 22b/22c are labelled Vulkan0-only (the harness skipped CPU); the 'ACTIVE on 98 tensors' load line is marked unreceipted; receipt 10's failed sibling (EXIT=2, the unconsumed SXT1 trailer), receipt 12's two runs, receipt 21's missing rc and script, and 13b's EXIT=1 binary-in-use build (leaving test-sx8-pca.exe pre-fix) are all named. The owed list gains the 27B PPL cell, the tied-head placement cost, --mode inplace's hard-coded qwen35 arch, the 3-D cur assert, the paired per-chunk NLL dump, and a built and stamped companion.

